NON CARGO.Report:
Keluhan Pax Transit
 Chorology Handling.
 On 05 February 2026, a transit passenger from flight KL835 continued their journey on GA714 to Sydney. During transit monitoring, a staff member captured a photograph of the passenger strictly for internal operational coordination purposes. The intent was to:
 - Confirm that the transit handling process had been completed;
 - Provide situational awareness to the operational team that the passenger was within the correct transit flow;
 - Mitigate the risk of a missing passenger during boarding.

NON CARGO.Preventive Action:
To strengthen governance and prevent recurrence, the following measures will be
 implemented:
 - An immediate re-briefing session will be conducted with the involved personnel to reinforce compliance standards and clarify the appropriate scope of authority;
 - Privacy awareness and data protection principles will be reinforced across the team;
 - Internal controls governing the use of operational documentation will be strengthened;
 - Passenger photographs will not be used for routine operational updates unless explicitly required by regulatory or security obligations.
